    "text": "In a photoelectric effect experiment, the threshold wavelength of light is<math><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>380</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> . If the wavelength of incident light is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>260</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> , the maximum kinetic energy of emitted electrons will be<br />Given <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math> (in <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> ) <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1237</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math>",
